{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"analogical-dashing-fennecfox","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nFour tests in tests/unit/test_subcall_class_selection.py each call _run_request_sites and reparse the entire src/rebar tree. Current macOS CI spends 30.10s, 32.27s, 31.02s, and 32.50s in the four guards in one contended run. A profiled local run observed four calls, 32,124 ast.parse calls, 34,004 reads, and 84.13s; a temporary process-local cache produced identical results with one call, 8,033 parses, 8,786 reads, and 23.26s. The original functional behavior is owned by closed ticket sand-dominating-urus; this ticket changes no invariant.\n\n## Plan\nCompute the immutable provenance analysis once per test process/module and share its result across the four independent assertions. Preserve all four assertions, registrations, and full-tree coverage.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] _run_request_sites executes once per test process for the four guards.\n- [ ] Every existing guard and offender diagnostic remains unchanged in meaning.\n- [ ] A defect-seeded raw-config site is still caught.\n- [ ] The cache cannot survive source changes across pytest sessions.","id":"fa90-3292-38d4-4fd2","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["ci","performance","tests","llm"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Four model-provenance guards repeat the same whole-tree AST analysis"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786598869895791001,"uuid":"f2807268-70fd-4ada-945d-d3763c3f5321"}